# Topic access per user (users and passwords: users.sh). Anything not listed is denied.

# ESPresense nodes: their own tree (rooms/, devices/, settings/ with enrolled phones' IRKs) and
# Home Assistant discovery, which they publish by default.
user espresense
topic readwrite espresense/#
topic readwrite homeassistant/#

# apps/presence: reads Bluetooth sightings.
user presence
topic read espresense/#

# apps/homeassistant: MQTT discovery and its status topic; reads ESPresense's states (the nodes'
# discovery entries point there) but cannot change node settings. Devices on other topics
# (zigbee2mqtt/#, shellies/#, …) need a line here first.
user homeassistant
topic readwrite homeassistant/#
topic read espresense/#

# The Ruuvi Gateway at the cabin: publishes ruuvi/<gateway MAC>/<tag MAC> (one reading) and
# ruuvi/<gateway MAC>/gw_status (online/offline, retained; offline is its last will).
user ruuvigateway
topic write ruuvi/#

# apps/ruuvi: reads the readings for Prometheus.
user ruuvi
topic read ruuvi/#
